From 17027fe4d9f7cc0a809da98bac53d355d7088330 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahyildiz <87144467+Ahyildiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:47:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 78/81] Ambient: drop the bluer kind of violet probe garbage
 before the raise

The probes' resolve can leave violet leftovers from other memory in the
light image; the magenta filter already here leaves the bluer kind (blue
over 2.5x green and over red) as a faint violet, a purple-blue glow on
bright surfaces (a lit sheet of paper in the prison cell cutscene). Sky
light (green above 0.4x blue) and sunsets (low blue) are not touched.

(cherry picked from trustno1-coder/VIctory-NVIDIA 826ba150, the second line;
the first is in VIctory-RDNA already)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6tkVHCftUUQbGm5NirGaG
---
 crates/victory-gpu/src/ambient.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/victory-gpu/src/ambient.rs b/crates/victory-gpu/src/ambient.rs
index ecdadf9..b8bf871 100644
--- a/crates/victory-gpu/src/ambient.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-gpu/src/ambient.rs
@@ -451,6 +451,12 @@ void raise(uint3 at : SV_DispatchThreadID) {
     float3 was = unpack(light[p]);
     // Filter magenta garbage probes left by uninitialized/corrupted memory on AMD.
     if (was.g < 0.5 * min(was.r, was.b) && max(was.r, was.b) > 0.02) was = 0.0;
+    // And the bluer kind of it (blue over 2.5x green and over red): left as
+    // a faint violet by the line above (a purple-blue glow on a lit sheet of
+    // paper in the prison cell, Ahyildiz in trustno1-coder/VIctory-NVIDIA
+    // 826ba150). The sky's light keeps green above 0.4x blue, sunsets keep
+    // blue low, so neither is touched.
+    if (was.b > 2.5 * was.g && was.b > was.r && was.b > 0.02) was = 0.0;
     float left = dot(was, LUMA);
     // What the program left counts as far as it can be true: the sky's light
     // outdoors, not the blocks of other memory.
